{"availability":"available","full":"hftsoi/symbolfit","name":"symbolfit","description":"Automatic parametric modeling with symbolic regression","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":75,"forks":6,"created":"2024-10-01T04:50:31Z","updated":"2026-10-05T22:56:41Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://hftsoi.github.io/symbolfit/","topics":["curve-fitting","high-energy-physics","lmfit","machine-learning","nonlinear-optimization","parametric-modelling","pysr","python","symbolic-regression","uncertainty-estimations"],"demo":"https://hftsoi.github.io/symbolfit/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:35.435Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:35.435Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:35.435Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T04:52:35.435Z","stars":75,"forks":6}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Docs | Paper | Slides | Colab | pip | conda |","SymbolFit automatically finds closed-form functions that fit your data with uncertainty estimation, no manual guessing required.","SymbolFit was originally developed for experimental high-energy physics (HEP) analyses, but it works on any 1D, 2D, or higher-dimensional dataset where you need an interpretable parametric model with uncertainty estimates. You provide data points and SymbolFit returns a batch of candidate functions ranked by goodness-of-fit, each with optimized parameters and uncertainty estimates. All results are saved to CSV tables and PDF plots, ready for downstream use such as hypothesis testing in HEP."],"features":["Function search: PySR (symbolic regression) explores combinations of mathematical operators to discover functional forms that fit the data, without requiring a predefined template.","Re-optimization: LMFIT re-optimizes the numerical parameters in each candidate function and provides uncertainty estimates via covariance matrices.","Evaluation: every candidate is automatically scored (chi2/NDF, p-value, RMSE, R2), plotted with individual uncertainty variations and total uncertainty coverage, and saved to output files."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hftsoi/symbolfit/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0f5311e52a096e93c6be6ac54194008b286f0544737e48ea9d2be95766378ff7","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:35.650Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:35.650Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Docs | Paper | Slides | Colab | pip | conda |","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hftsoi/symbolfit/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"0f5311e52a096e93c6be6ac54194008b286f0544737e48ea9d2be95766378ff7","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hftsoi/symbolfit/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:35.650Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-05T22:56:41Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hftsoi/symbolfit/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:35.651Z","hash":"0f5311e52a096e93c6be6ac54194008b286f0544737e48ea9d2be95766378ff7","originalBytes":9862,"storedBytes":9862,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["pysr","fit","uncertainty","symbolfit","data","config","output","max","python","arxiv","candidate","conda","dir","down","example","functions","installation","set","candidates","dataset","each","import","results","automatically","bin","documentation","false","histograms","input","model","none","operators","own","parameters","physics","run","science","tsoi","author","chi2","citation","complexity","computer","cranmer","csv","dataset.y","default","different","docs","function","goodness-of-fit","here","loss","machine","miles","only","parameter","parametric","pdf","scale","simply","slides","symbolic","title","uncertainties","version","via","weights","widths","year","archiveprefix","astrophysics","batch","caillol","cecile","clone","colab","covariance","dasu","demo","discover","doi","duarte","dylan","elliot","env","eprint","estimates.","etc.","explores","files","first","format","full","fung","harri